<title>USA: Granite sets $150 million private offering.</title>
<headline>Granite sets $150 million private offering.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Granite Broadcasting Corp said on Tuesday it plans a $150 million private offering of a new class of Cumulative Exchangeable Preferred Stock due 2009 in order to complete its acquisition of WXON-TV, the WB affiliate serving Detroit, Michigan.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale, together with borrowings under an existing $200 million credit facility, will be used to fund the $175 million cash purchase price for WXON-TV.  The acquisition was announced in December.</p>
</text>
